      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T20:23:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems odd that there\u0027s a sysfs entry for a dm driver, but we\u0027re not supposed to use it.\n\nThe file is used to read and write the state of the device - it can be in TRIM, CHECKPOINT or COMMITTED state. There might well be better ways of doing this, but not without breaking user space.\n\nI mean I can (and will) add documentation, but I don\u0027t think that\u0027s the core of the problem here.",
      "parentUuid": "f45ab60f_b5900357",
      "revId": "ae356ab1038e245b717920f8dcd987d2d9266505",
